  "answer": "SBCERS scores respondents to its global custody RFP on four criteria:\n\n| Evaluation criterion | Weight |\n|---|---:|\n| Scope affirmation, servicing approach, and institutional credentials | 30% |\n| Core and value-added services and technology platforms | 40% |\n| Quality of responses and additional evidence of capability | 5% |\n| Competitiveness and reasonableness of economics | 25% |\n\nFees are assessed relative to service quality; SBCERS is **not required to select the lowest-cost respondent**. Source: [SBCERS Global Custody RFP, Section V, p. 27](SBCERS__01_2023-SBCERS-Custody-RFP-CONSOLIDATED-Final-Updated.pdf#page=27).",
